# Build output is COMMITTED on purpose.
#
# This package declares no `prepare`/`postinstall` hook, so consumers get
# `build/` straight from the git checkout. That is deliberate: pnpm hard-errors
# on git deps that need unapproved build scripts (ERR_PNPM_GIT_DEP_PREPARE_NOT_ALLOWED),
# and bun blocks dependency lifecycle scripts unless the user opts in with
# `bun pm trust`. A `prepare` hook would also force every consumer to download
# this package's devDependencies just to run `tsc`.
#
# To change the sources:
#   1. edit src/
#   2. npm run build      (or: bun run build)
#   3. commit both src/ and build/ together
#
# (the rule itself lives at the bottom of this file, commented out)

# Dependencies
node_modules/

